       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single dose is usually capped at about 850\u20131,000 mg. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is substantial.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is a more conservative option.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, for example because of a specific protocol, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
